 ## Background
-The AABB Face Normal Test is a fundamental component of the Separating Axis Theorem (SAT) applied to axis-aligned boxes. It exploits the property that the normals of an AABB are parallel to the coordinate axes. By translating the AABB center to the origin, the projection test simplifies to comparing vertex extents against half-extents. This approach is widely used in real-time rendering, voxelization, and collision detection systems where performance is critical. The specific implementation details described here are derived from GPU-based voxelization techniques [S1].
